  "case": {
    "id": "CASE-10759",
    "title": "A plugin's dependency hoists dsh-tools@0.2.0-rc.2 into the profile, so the in-box `tools` row is disabled and the host cannot boot",
    "source": {
      "kind": "github-discussion",
      "url": "https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/discussions/10759",
      "author": "WhichWitchWin",
      "reported_at": "2026-10-23",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-10-26",
      "evidence_tier": "declared"
    },
    "reported": {
      "plugin": "@deepseek-ai/dsh-tools",
      "plugin_version": "0.2.0-rc.2",
      "runtime_before": "0.2.1-rc.2",
      "runtime_after": "0.2.1-rc.2",
      "symptom": "after `dsh plugin --profile desktop add dsh-livedocs` the window flashes and exits; `1 required plugin did not activate`, `agent-loop (required) → tools missing`; then DSH resets the profile (bundles → base+web-app, cordis.patch.yml → []) and every third-party plugin disappears",
      "runtime_trace": "dsh: disabling profile plugin row \"tools\": Plugin @deepseek-ai/dsh-tools@0.2.0-rc.2 is incompatible with dsh 0.2.1-rc.2: requirements {\"@deepseek-ai/dsh-agent\":\"0.2.0-rc.2\", ...}",
      "user_hypotheses": [
        "the runtime package is simply missing (it is not: it is shadowed by the profile copy)",
        "reinstalling the plugin fixes it (it does not: the hoisted copy comes back)"
      ],
      "root_cause": "dsh-livedocs declares @deepseek-ai/dsh-tools in dependencies (not peerDependencies), so pnpm materialises 0.2.0-rc.2 at <profile>/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh-tools; the resolved row module then fails the version rule against the 0.2.1-rc.2 runtime",
      "fix_verified_by_reporter": "not stated by the reporter; the thread documents the boot-failure → profile-reset chain"
    },
    "deviations": [
      "the `tools` row belongs to the in-box `@deepseek-ai/dsh-base` bundle, not to the profile patch; it is re-mounted in the profile patch layer so the case stays a one-row reconstruction (profile rows and bundle rows resolve through the same resolver, so the attribution is unchanged)",
      "bundles omitted: dsh-base / dsh-web-app are left out to keep the composition minimal",
      "the hoisting plugin's own version (`dsh-livedocs`) is not stated in the report, so its manifest is not reproduced; only the copy it produces (dsh-tools@0.2.0-rc.2, the module the row actually resolves to) is materialised",
      "the report was written before dsh-tools@0.2.1-rc.x was published; the input is the 0.2.0-rc.2 manifest the message names, not today's newest",
      "the profile reset (bundles → 2, cordis.patch.yml → []) is a separate defect and is not modelled"
    ],
    "reproduced": {
      "dsh_home": "~\\home",
      "profile": "desktop",
      "bundles": []
    }
  },
